[gd_scene format=3]

; The Mere, east of the Coldstacks' lower corridor (map offset (278.5, -79)): a frozen lake in a low cavern. The
; pilgrim walks out on the ice; two leads of open black water break it, and through the cut of the lake (its front,
; seen from the side) the water goes down twenty meters to a bed of rock. Without Ballast the pilgrim floats in a lead
; and climbs out; with it, it sinks to the lake bed, where a shaft goes on down into the Underice (Ballast both ways).
; Choristers kneel asleep on the ice; a hard landing wakes them. East, the shore rises to the Sounding's door.

